From: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: clear stale Brick suspend token in SPL

A deep-suspend resume enters BL31 directly and does not execute SPL. A full
boot always executes SPL before BL31, so clear the retained resume token
there. This prevents a watchdog or cold reset after an interrupted suspend
from being mistaken for a warm resume.

Signed-off-by: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
index b54efea..af5cd42 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -475,6 +475,18 @@ u32 spl_mmc_boot_mode(struct mmc *mmc, const u32 boot_device)
 	return result;
 }
 
+static void trimui_brick_clear_suspend_token(void)
+{
+	void __iomem *token = (void __iomem *)0x07000100;
+
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_TRIMUI_BRICK_SD_DIAGNOSTIC))
+		return;
+
+	writel(0, token);
+	/* Complete the always-on-domain write before BL31 can inspect it. */
+	(void)readl(token);
+}
+
 void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 {
 	sunxi_sram_init();
@@ -483,5 +495,7 @@ void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 	timer_init();
 	clock_init();
+	trimui_brick_clear_suspend_token();
+
 	gpio_init();
 
 	spl_init();
